WEBVTT

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:06.000
<v Juan Sequeda>All right, we're wrapping up. What's your advice about data, about life?

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:15.000
<v Ada Park>Start with the questions your business actually asks. Knowledge graphs only pay off when they answer real questions.

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:20.000
<v Ada Park>And read Designing Data-Intensive Applications, it changed how I think about data modeling.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:24.000
<v Tim Gasper>Love that. Who should we invite next?

00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:33.000
<v Ada Park>You should invite Ben Ortiz, he thinks deeply about semantics. And also Grace Hopper Lee from Acme Graph.

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:36.000
<v Juan Sequeda>Great picks.

00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:40.000
<v Ada Park>Oh, and Hana Sato too.

00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:52.000
<v Tim Gasper>Awesome. What resources do you follow? Thank you so much Ada, this has been an amazing conversation about knowledge graphs and questions and we will see everyone next week.
